15 0 obj
<< /A 39 0 R /Alt (Flowchart illustrates the process for predicting imipenem exposure and adjusting pediatric doses in renal impairment, detailing input optimization, parameter adjustments, PBPK modeling for various renal functions, and verification steps.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 29 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 40 0 R /Alt (Nine-panel figure of line graphs labeled A through I, each showing drug concentration in micrograms per milliliter versus time in hours for various intravenous dosing regimens. Pink data points and fitted curves illustrate pharmacokinetic profiles under different dosing conditions, including varying dosages, infusion durations, and bolus administrations. Panels H and I display repeated dosing over extended periods.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 41 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a line graph of drug concentration versus time for a 15 milligrams per kilogram, 0.5 hour intravenous drip; concentration rapidly peaks and then declines. Panel B displays the same for 25 milligrams per kilogram, 0.5 hour drip, showing higher peak concentrations. Panel C shows 15 milligrams per kilogram, 1 hour drip with a lower, broader peak. All graphs include observed data points and modeled concentration curves.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 42 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a line graph of drug concentration over time for mild renal impairment, panel B for moderate renal impairment, and panel C for severe renal impairment. All graphs plot concentration in micrograms per milliliter versus time in hours, with declining curves and data points, and axes labeled accordingly. Each panel features a central fitted curve with upper and lower confidence interval lines and pink squares representing observed data points.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 43 0 R /Alt (Two line graphs labeled A and B compare drug concentration over time for normal renal function, mild, moderate, and severe renal impairment, using black, green, red, and blue lines respectively. In both panels, higher severity of renal impairment results in increased and prolonged drug concentrations. Panel A shows a sharp peak followed by a rapid decline, while Panel B shows a steady rise to a plateau and a slower decline. Concentration is measured in micrograms per milliliter and time in hours.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 44 0 R /Alt (Panel A is a line graph showing attainment of PTA by MIC for normal renal function, mild, moderate, and severe renal impairment, with severe impairment maintaining higher PTA at elevated MIC. Panel B is a similar graph, where all groups maintain high PTA until a steep decline at MIC values above eight milligrams per liter. Panel C shows overlapping lines for all groups, with PTA remaining high and sharply decreasing at higher MIC values.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
